{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"73651a459f29dd7450c6c7cc39df246c43793a49"},"timestamp":1534199051,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMjY4NTY4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2768#issuecomment-412685684"},"message":"[GitMate.io](https://gitmate.io) thinks possibly related issues are https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/227 (datalad get  barfes), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1965 (datalad run fails to automatically get files within subdatasets), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865 (Performance issue of save() with many files), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2276 (datalad run  misses original files which were renamed and leaves them deleted), and https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2576 (Option to store run records in annexed sidecar files).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1534206379,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMjcxMTM3MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2768#issuecomment-412711370"},"message":"yeah, error reporting from underlying tools could be improved\n\n\u003e [ERROR  ] transfer already in progress, or unable to take transfer lock\n\nis by `git-annex` which \"rightfully\" locks to prevent multiple conflicting operations from happening.  If the behavior of \"wait for the lock\" (instead of \"fail if can't acquire a lock\") is **really** needed, I guess we could implement it one way (at git-annex level may be, @joeyh?) or another (in datalad).  The question would be -- wouldn't you keep piling up the processes waiting to get a lock?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1534206599,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMjcxMjAwNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2768#issuecomment-412712006"},"message":"\u003e I have been using Datalad a lot throughout the last 7 weeks and I really enjoyed my experience\n\nTHANK YOU and the feedback, and I'm really glad you found it enjoyable overall!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"e6d4813f22ddb02ab4ff047e0d9770a56e42fd25"},"timestamp":1534208381,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMjcxNzE1NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2768#issuecomment-412717155"},"message":"If the operation holding the lock is a `get` (I noticed that `update` and `publish` locks were confliting, but they weren't conflicting with `get` so I do not know if the `get`operation has its own independant lock), the idea I had was not that the second `get` should wait for the lock, but should wait for the `get` completion.\n\nIn other words, if two threads or processes try to perform `datalad get` on the same file, the thread that requested it second would only wait for the first thread to finish the `get` operation and would then use its result as its own (meaning only 1 actual `get` would have been issued in total). In that sense, maybe an option could be added to force the release of the lock so that, when the second thread tries to issue the `datalad get`, it would interrupt the first thread and initiate its own `get`.\n\nAs with some other issues I opened earlier this week, I am unsure if this is actually something that should or even could be implemented at the Datalad level. I haven't investigated to see if git-annex offers such an option, but I suppose such a feature would probably make more sense directly in there than in Datalad. It may also be much easier to implement there.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1534255230,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMjg4MTc4OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2768#issuecomment-412881788"},"message":"I've pondered before making git-annex wait for transfer locks rather\nthan failing, at least as an option.\n\nOne problem with it is that if a process gets suspended with ctrl-z,\nunrelated commands will hang.\n\nWhen git-annex is configured to use a pid lock, there is no fine-grained\nlocking, so any transfer would wait on any other transfer -- but the\nsame lack of fine grained locking currently makes any second transfer\n(by a different process) fail.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"a2318fd593c7dcad413bfba96a1967f9958e040b"},"timestamp":1556849040,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4ODg5MjY3Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2768#issuecomment-488892676"},"message":"Is this problem fixed?\n How can I restart a failed one?\n\n\u003eTotal (4 ok, 16 failed out of 149)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1556850040,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4ODg5NzIzOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2768#issuecomment-488897238"},"message":"For failed one, just rerun and it will try fetch they ones still missing if any left","files":null}]}